---
// Fixed array value copy vs dynamic Slice view (ptr, len, cap), append growth, and preallocation.
const W = 900;
const H = 288;
---
<figure class="gf2a">
  <div class="gf2a-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Comparison of fixed Go arrays versus dynamic slices backed by an underlying array, capacity growth steps during append, and zero-reallocation make preallocation.">
      {/* Left card: Array vs Slice anatomy */}
      <rect x="14" y="14" width="428" height="260" rx="10" class="gf2a-card" />
      <text x="30" y="42" class="gf2a-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>1. Array [4]int (Fixed) vs. Slice []int (View)</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>1. Mảng tĩnh [4]int vs. Slice động []int</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="60" width="396" height="58" rx="6" class="gf2a-box" />
      <text x="44" y="80" class="gf2a-b">Array: var a [4]int  (length baked into type!)</text>
      <text x="44" y="99" class="gf2a-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Fixed size [4]int != [5]int; assigning b := a copies all bytes.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Độ dài dính cứng vào kiểu; gán b := a copy toàn bộ phần tử.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="128" width="166" height="70" rx="6" class="gf2a-box is-ok" />
      <text x="42" y="149" class="gf2a-b-ok">Slice Header (24 B)</text>
      <text x="42" y="167" class="gf2a-m">ptr → backing array</text>
      <text x="42" y="185" class="gf2a-m">len = 3  |  cap = 4</text>

      <line x1="200" y1="163" x2="226" y2="163" class="gf2a-wire-ok" />
      <polygon points="232,163 224,158 224,168" class="gf2a-head-ok" />

      <rect x="236" y="128" width="190" height="70" rx="6" class="gf2a-box" />
      <text x="248" y="149" class="gf2a-b">Backing Array [4]int</text>
      <text x="248" y="167" class="gf2a-m">[0]=10  [1]=20  [2]=30</text>
      <text x="248" y="185" class="gf2a-b-ok">[3]=spare slot (len &lt; cap)</text>

      <rect x="30" y="210" width="396" height="48" rx="6" class="gf2a-box" />
      <text x="44" y="230" class="gf2a-b">copy(dst, src) breaks aliasing cleanly</text>
      <text x="44" y="246" class="gf2a-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Copies min(len(dst), len(src)) into an independent array.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Chép phần tử sang mảng mới tách biệt hoàn toàn khi cần cắt rời.</tspan>
      </text>

      {/* Right card: append() capacity growth vs preallocation */}
      <rect x="460" y="14" width="426" height="260" rx="10" class="gf2a-card" />
      <text x="476" y="42" class="gf2a-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>2. append() growth vs. make([]int, 0, n)</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>2. Cơ chế phình sức chứa append() vs. cấp phát trước</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="476" y="60" width="394" height="84" rx="6" class="gf2a-box is-red" />
      <text x="490" y="80" class="gf2a-b-red">Naive: var s []int; for i &lt; 10 {'{'} s = append(s, i) {'}'}</text>
      <text x="490" y="100" class="gf2a-m">Go 1.27 measured cap jumps: 1 → 2 → 4 → 8 → 16</text>
      <text x="490" y="120" class="gf2a-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Every full resize allocates a bigger array + copies old items!</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Mỗi lần tràn cap phải xin mảng mới ở Heap rồi chép lại toàn bộ.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="476" y="156" width="394" height="102" rx="6" class="gf2a-box is-ok" />
      <text x="490" y="177" class="gf2a-b-ok">Idiomatic: pre := make([]int, 0, 10)</text>
      <text x="490" y="198" class="gf2a-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>len = 0 (starts empty!), cap = 10 reserved up front.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>len = 0 (rỗng sẵn sàng cho append), cap = 10 giữ chỗ trước.</tspan>
      </text>
      <text x="490" y="218" class="gf2a-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Appending 0..9 fits cleanly in 1 allocation with zero copies.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Đẩy đủ 10 phần tử chỉ mất đúng 1 lần cấp phát, 0 lần copy lại.</tspan>
      </text>
      <text x="490" y="238" class="gf2a-b-ok">Trap: make([]int, 10) adds 10 zeroes → append jumps to [10]!</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Arrays in Go are fixed-length values, while slices are lightweight 24-byte views (ptr, len, cap). Preallocating capacity with make([]T, 0, n) avoids repeated array copies during append().</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Array trong Go cố định kích thước và copy cả cục, còn Slice là cửa sổ 24-byte (ptr, len, cap) linh hoạt. Dùng make([]T, 0, n) đặt sẵn sức chứa giúp append() chạy mượt mà không tốn công nhân bản mảng.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gf2a { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gf2a-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gf2a svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .gf2a text { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .gf2a-card { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gf2a-box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gf2a-box.is-red { stroke: var(--red); fill: var(--red-tint-bg); }
  .gf2a-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gf2a-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gf2a-h { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gf2a-b { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gf2a-b-red { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .gf2a-b-ok { font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gf2a-b-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gf2a-m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .gf2a-wire-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); stroke-width: 1.8; }
  .gf2a-head-ok { fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gf2a-wire-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gf2a-head-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gf2a figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
